// Streams :
// Streams in Java were introduced in Java 8 as part of the java.util.stream package. A Stream is used to process collections
// of data such as lists, sets, and arrays in a simple and efficient manner. Streams help developers perform operations like filtering,
// sorting, searching, mapping, and collecting data with less code and better readability.

