// Features of stream:

// 1.Streams Do Not Store Data : 
//   Streams do not have their own storage. They process data from collections such as List, Set, or Array.

  //List<Integer> list = Arrays.asList(1,2,3);
  //Stream<Integer> stream = list.stream();

// 2.Streams support pipeline processing :
//   Streams allow multiple operations to be connected together in sequence. This sequence is called a stream pipeline.
//   pipline Structue : Source → Intermediate Operations → Terminal Operation

// 3.Streams are lazy :
//   Intermediate operations do not execute immediately. Execution starts only after terminal operation is called. This behavior is called lazy execution.
//   Example:
//     IntStream.of(1,2,3)
//              .filter(n -> n > 1);
//     Nothing executes here................

//     IntStream.of(1,2,3)
//          .filter(n -> n > 1)
//          .count();
//     Now execution starts because terminal method count()..


// 4.Streams Support Parallel Processing :
//   Streams can process data using multiple threads simultaneously. This is called parallel stream processing.

// 5.Streams Support Functional Programming :
//   Streams use functional programming concepts. Operations are written using lambda expressions, method references.


